# cmd.exe requires CRLF line endings in .bat/.cmd files. It streams a batch file from
# disk by byte offset and re-seeks after every command; with LF-only endings it
# mis-locates line boundaries and execution jumps into the middle of unrelated blocks.
#
# This matters here because script.bat SELF-UPDATES from
# https://github.com/.../archive/refs/heads/master.zip. GitHub builds that zip with
# `git archive` using server-side defaults (core.autocrlf unset), so without this
# attribute the zip ships the LF-normalised blob and the launcher overwrites the user's
# working CRLF script.bat with an LF-only one. The next run then executes a batch file
# cmd.exe cannot parse -- the run jumps between unrelated error blocks and never reaches
# the orchestrator. `eol=crlf` makes `git archive` emit CRLF regardless of the server's
# config, so the self-updated copy stays runnable.
#
# Do NOT remove this, and do NOT let a `* text=auto` rule above it win.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
